<% identity = Rails.configuration.x.foundation %>
<article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-6 leading-relaxed">
  <header>
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-md-on-surface-variant">
      Version <%= Foundation::Legal.terms_label %>
      &middot; Last updated <%= Foundation::Legal::TERMS_UPDATED_ON.iso8601 %>
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 rounded-md border border-md-tertiary bg-md-tertiary-container px-4 py-3 text-sm text-md-on-tertiary-container">
      This is a live demo deployment of the Pomodoro timer, provided for
      evaluation only. It is not a commercial service. Before any production
      launch, the operator must complete the operator details noted at the end
      of this document and have qualified counsel review it.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms of Service (the "Terms") are an agreement between you and
      the operator of <%= identity[:application_name] %> (the "Service").
      The Service is a focus timer: it runs Pomodoro work and break intervals
      in your browser. Questions about these Terms can be sent to
      <%= mail_to identity[:legal_email], nil, class: "underline underline-offset-2" %>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">2. What the Service is</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is a web application reachable at
      https://<%= identity[:domain] %> and at pages linked from it. It runs a
      Pomodoro timer entirely in your browser — work sessions (default 25
      minutes), short breaks (5 minutes), and a long break (15 minutes) after
      every four work sessions. The timer works without an account; signing in
      adds a personal history of your completed sessions.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Service evolves: features may be added, changed, or retired.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">3. Accounts and eligibility</h2>
    <p>
      You must be at least 16 years old to create an account, or older where
      the law of your residence sets a higher minimum for agreeing to terms
      like these. By creating an account you confirm that you meet this
      requirement.
    </p>
    <p>
      You agree to provide a working email address, keep your credentials
      secret, and tell us promptly at
      <%= mail_to identity[:support_email], nil, class: "underline underline-offset-2" %>
      if you believe your account has been accessed without your permission.
      You are responsible for activity performed with your credentials until
      you notify us. Accounts are for a single person; registering with
      disposable email addresses is not permitted.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">4. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>When using the Service you agree not to:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
      <li>break the law, or help anyone else break it;</li>
      <li>probe, scan, overload, or attempt to bypass security or rate limits, including CAPTCHA or bot challenges;</li>
      <li>scrape or bulk-collect content or personal data without written permission;</li>
      <li>impersonate another person or misrepresent your affiliation;</li>
      <li>harass, threaten, or defraud other users.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We may remove content or suspend accounts that we reasonably believe
      violate this section, with notice where practical.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">5. Your content and our IP</h2>
    <p>
      Session history you generate — your completed focus and break sessions —
      belongs to you. You grant the operator a worldwide, non-exclusive
      license to store and process it solely to run the Service. This license
      ends when the data is deleted, except for lawful backups kept for a
      limited time.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Service itself — its software, design, trademarks, and content the
      operator provides — belongs to the operator or its licensors. Open
      source components remain governed by their own licenses. Except for
      rights these Terms grant expressly, no rights in the Service are
      transferred to you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">6. Purchases and refunds</h2>
    <p>
      The Service currently offers no paid products or subscriptions. If
      paid features are introduced later, prices and currency will be shown at
      the point of purchase and charged through a payment processor, and the
      checkout page will always show the amount you will pay before you
      confirm.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">7. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
    <p>
      The Service is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of
      any kind, express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose.
      We do not warrant that the Service will be uninterrupted, secure, or
      error-free. A timer interruption, missed break, or lost session history
      is your own responsibility to manage.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">8. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, the operator is not liable for
      indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or
      for lost profits or data, arising from your use of the Service.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">9. Termination</h2>
    <p>
      You may stop using the Service at any time and delete your account and
      session history. We may suspend or terminate access to the Service if we
      reasonably believe you have violated these Terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">10. Changes to these Terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these Terms from time to time. The current version is
      always available at https://<%= identity[:domain] %>/legal/terms, with
      the "Last updated" date shown at the top. Continued use of the Service
      after changes take effect means you accept the updated Terms.
    </p>
  </section>

